// Golden fixtures for the trip document, WRITTEN BY THE WEB: each was produced
// by running `src/shared/roadtrip/trip-types.ts` itself (`migrateTripDoc`,
// the factories, and a realistic v28 trip composed with the web's own
// factories) under node's type stripping, with `crypto.randomUUID` replaced
// by a counter (`f1`, `f2`… building a fixture, `m1`… migrating it,
// `k1`… in a factory, `r1`… composing the realistic trip) and `Date.now`
// pinned to 1 750 000 000 000. The Swift side replays the same counters, so
// a migrated trip, a factory's record and a web-written trip must come out
// here as the SAME JSON, key for key — not merely "close".
//
// What they pin that the ported spec (`TripTypesTests.swift`) does not:
// JavaScript's semantics on a stored value of the wrong type (no version runs
// no step; a version written as text is a number; an empty shade list is
// TRUE; a strength written as text crosses as text; a route option written
// null is `Number(null)` = 0; an empty hook list is refilled), and the exact
// shape every writer emits.
//
// To regenerate after a change on the web: node 22 runs the TypeScript as it
// is (`node --experimental-strip-types --import <register.mjs> gen.ts`) once a
// module resolve hook retries an extensionless relative import with `.ts`
// appended; no `node_modules` is needed, since these modules import nothing
// but each other at run time.

